        "body": "Anthropic is a San Francisco-based AI startup founded in 2021. The company describes Claude as its AI, built for problem solvers to tackle complex challenges, analyze data, write code, and think through difficult work. Claude is available as a general LLM assistant through the chat interface at claude.ai.\n\nAnthropic offers Claude through multiple product interfaces including the Anthropic Console for API management, prompt testing, evaluation tools, usage monitoring, and cost controls. The company also provides Claude Code for agentic coding capabilities and Computer Use, a computer control agent for desktop automation and system access. An MCP server for LLM orchestration with Langchain Anthropic is registered in the company's ecosystem.\n\nThe company faces multiple ongoing lawsuits. Cases are pending in federal courts including the Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit (Edelson, PC, et al. v. Anthropic, PBC) and district courts across California, Vermont, Hawaii, Delaware, and Pennsylvania. The company has significant legal exposure, with 208 cases registered to California jurisdiction.",
